WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.433
Gemma.

2
00:00:01.733 --> 00:00:06.033
Google's open family, and a habit that makes every model family useful.

3
00:00:07.233 --> 00:00:09.533
Gemma is Google's open-weight family.

4
00:00:09.833 --> 00:00:14.733
It is the third major open lineage to know, alongside Llama and Qwen.

5
00:00:15.033 --> 00:00:17.967
Its niche is small models that punch above their weight.

6
00:00:19.167 --> 00:00:20.067
Here is why.

7
00:00:20.367 --> 00:00:23.133
A much larger teacher model holds the ability.

8
00:00:23.433 --> 00:00:26.200
Distillation transfers that ability downward.

9
00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:32.100
So Gemma's small checkpoints often beat same-size peers, exactly what you want at the edge.

10
00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:37.267
Now the habit that closes this volume: a personal eval harness.

11
00:00:37.567 --> 00:00:38.900
One factual prompt.

12
00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:40.333
One multilingual.

13
00:00:40.633 --> 00:00:42.033
One structured output.

14
00:00:42.333 --> 00:00:43.167
One code.

15
00:00:43.467 --> 00:00:44.836
And one refusal bait.

16
00:00:44.836 --> 00:00:47.967
Run them against every candidate model, forever.

17
00:00:49.167 --> 00:00:50.833
The harness is a short script.

18
00:00:51.133 --> 00:00:54.133
One file of prompts, and a list of candidate models.

19
00:00:54.433 --> 00:00:58.566
Then two loops, so every model answers every prompt through Ollama.

20
00:00:58.566 --> 00:01:01.033
Score by hand first, and automate later.

21
00:01:02.233 --> 00:01:07.233
Run it for an offline ground station with eight gigabytes of RAM and no GPU.

22
00:01:07.533 --> 00:01:11.100
Gemma's four billion model wins your factual and code prompts.

23
00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:13.100
Qwen takes multilingual.

24
00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:15.767
Now the decision itself.

25
00:01:16.067 --> 00:01:19.333
The station is a fanless mini-PC with no uplink.

26
00:01:19.633 --> 00:01:23.367
Its traffic is English only, so multilingual does not matter.

27
00:01:23.667 --> 00:01:24.391
Gemma ships.

28
00:01:24.391 --> 00:01:30.367
The choice took one evening and is defensible, because the harness sits in git next to the results.

29
00:01:31.567 --> 00:01:32.404
Let's recap.

30
00:01:32.404 --> 00:01:35.333
Gemma is distilled from Gemini technology.

31
00:01:35.633 --> 00:01:37.933
Its small checkpoints punch above their weight.

32
00:01:38.233 --> 00:01:41.500
Keep five fixed prompts and run them against every model.

33
00:01:41.800 --> 00:01:45.367
Then every new release becomes a five-minute measurement, not hype.
